ArrayList → Default List (Most Used)
-----------------------------------
📌 Purpose
     Store ordered elements with fast access.
Why Industry Uses It
 ✔ Fast get(index) → O(1)
 ✔ Memory efficient
 ✔ Simple and predictable
 ✔ Cache-friendly
Used When
 API responses
 DB results
 DTO lists
In-memory data
UI data

ArrayDeque → Default Queue / Stack
-------------------------------------
📌 Purpose
    Fast FIFO / LIFO / double-ended operations.

Why Industry Uses It
 ✔ O(1) add/remove
 ✔ No node objects (unlike LinkedList)
 ✔ Faster than Stack & LinkedList
 ✔ Low GC pressure
Used When
  BFS / DFS
  Task queues
  Sliding window
  Undo/redo
  Request processing

PriorityQueue → Ranking / Scheduling
-------------------------------------
📌 Purpose
     Always get min/max element.

Why Industry Uses It
  ✔ O(log n) operations
  ✔ Best for top-K / scheduling
  ✔ Heap-based → efficient
Used When
  Job schedulers
  Dijkstra
  Load balancing
  Event systems
  Leaderboards
  Rate limiting

HashSet → Fast Unique Collection
📌 Purpose
    Store unique elements with fast lookup.

Why Industry Uses It
  ✔ O(1) contains/add
  ✔ No duplicates
  ✔ Very fast
Used When
  Removing duplicates
  Caching keys
  Permission lists
  Validation
  Filtering

Thread-safe versions

  | Normal        | Thread-Safe                   |
  | ------------- | ----------------------------- |
  | ArrayList     | CopyOnWriteArrayList          |
  | HashSet       | ConcurrentHashMap.newKeySet() |
  | ArrayDeque    | ConcurrentLinkedQueue         |
  | PriorityQueue | PriorityBlockingQueue         |

| Need             | Use                 |
| ---------------- | ------------------- |
| Ordered List     | ArrayList           |
| Fast Queue/Stack | ArrayDeque          |
| Priority         | PriorityQueue       |
| Unique Items     | HashSet             |
| Thread Safe      | Concurrent versions |


| Scenario              | Best Choice     | Why         |
| --------------------- | --------------- | ----------- |
| Add/remove at end     | `ArrayList`     | Fastest     |
| Add/remove front/back | `ArrayDeque`    | O(1)        |
| Add/remove middle     | `LinkedList`    | No shifting |
| Unique + fast remove  | `HashSet`       | Hashing     |
| Priority-based remove | `PriorityQueue` | Heap        |
